Subject: [PATCH] Document the section store a template folder gets

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/main/java/athena/api/Athena.java b/src/main/java/athena/api/Athena.java
index 151be5551a6b9b44bc9ccfee66a48cc8a7e74763..e3d07a01ec2b6eb811dab97f8b919f5aa7aced11 100644
--- a/src/main/java/athena/api/Athena.java
+++ b/src/main/java/athena/api/Athena.java
@@ -18,9 +18,9 @@ import org.bukkit.entity.Player;
  *
  * <h2>Template worlds</h2>
  *
- * A template world is loaded from a map folder that stays exactly as it is: no copy, no unzip,
+ * A template world is loaded from a map folder that stays as it is: no copy, no unzip,
  * no {@code session.lock}, no {@code uid.dat}, and no chunk, player or level data is ever saved into
- * it. Several worlds - on this server or on other servers of the same machine - can use one
+ * it (the one file added is a cache of its sections; see below). Several worlds - on this server or on other servers of the same machine - can use one
  * template at once, and the operating system's file cache holds the map's files once for all of
  * them.
  * <ul>
@@ -36,6 +36,13 @@ import org.bukkit.entity.Player;
  *       under different names.</li>
  *   <li>Unload it with {@link org.bukkit.Server#unloadWorld(World, boolean)} as usual once no
  *       player is left in it.</li>
+ *   <li>The one file the server adds to the folder is {@code athena-sections-<fingerprint>.bin},
+ *       built in the background the first time the template loads: the map's block ids and light
+ *       in a form the server reads in place from the file cache, so later loads keep almost none of
+ *       them on the Java heap. It is rebuilt whenever the region files change; the folder needs to
+ *       be writable for it, and without it the map loads onto the heap as before. Never overwrite
+ *       it in place while a server runs (cp, scp): copy maps with a tool that replaces files by
+ *       renaming them, such as rsync.</li>
  * </ul>
  *
  * <h2>Teleports</h2>
